/// \class BoneFXUpdateModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_update_module_factories_a
/// \brief Module data for BoneFXUpdate: FX lists, object creation lists and
///        particle systems to play at model bones, per body damage state.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// BoneFXUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData and shared by every object
/// of the template. It is by far the largest data class in this group,
/// because it holds every slot below. The module itself, BoneFXUpdate, is registered with
/// BoneFXUpdate::friend_newModuleInstance, which this group does not
/// document.
///
/// \par Modding
/// INI fields, read from the retail table; the names match Zero Hour's:
/// - \c DamageFXTypes, \c DamageOCLTypes and \c DamageParticleTypes, sets
///   of damage type names parsed by INI::parseDamageTypeFlags;
/// - for each of the four damage states Pristine, Damaged, ReallyDamaged
///   and Rubble, eight numbered slots of each kind: \c PristineFXList1 to
///   \c PristineFXList8 (parsed by BoneFXUpdateModuleData::parseFXList),
///   \c PristineOCL1 to \c PristineOCL8 (parsed by
///   BoneFXUpdateModuleData::parseObjectCreationList) and
///   \c PristineParticleSystem1 to \c PristineParticleSystem8, and likewise
///   for the other three states.
///
/// The eight slots per state and kind are fixed by the table: a ninth
/// numbered field does not exist. Zero Hour has the same limit
/// (\c BONE_FX_MAX_BONES); Zero Hour: each slot names a bone, a random
/// delay range and whether the effect plays only once.

/// \fn ModuleData *BoneFXUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "BoneFXUpdate": builds the module
///        data for one module line and parses its INI block.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration
/// while an `Object` block is read. It constructs BoneFXUpdateModuleData
/// with its defaults, then, when \p ini is not null, parses the block with
/// INI::initFromINIMultiProc and BoneFXUpdateModuleData::buildFieldParse,
/// which registers the class's one table.
///
/// \param ini  The INI reader positioned at the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see BoneFXUpdateModuleData


