/// \class DamageFieldUpdate
/// \ingroup grp_w1023_update_module_factories_a
/// \brief Weapon-firing update registered as "DamageFieldUpdate", with a
///        radius, an object filter and a required upgrade.
///
/// Its constructor runs FireWeaponUpdate's constructor first, so it is built
/// on FireWeaponUpdate. Its registration pairs it with
/// DamageFieldUpdateModuleData::friend_newModuleData, which this group does
/// not document. That data's DamageFieldUpdateModuleData::buildFieldParse
/// registers FireWeaponUpdateModuleData::buildFieldParse's table first and
/// then its own. Neither Zero Hour nor Open-BFME-1's \c game/ tree has the
/// class. The module's logic is not described here.
